Package: scf
Title: Analyzing the Survey of Consumer Finances
Version: 1.0.1
Authors@R:
    c(person("Joseph","Cohen", role = c("aut","cre"),
             email = "joseph.cohen@qc.cuny.edu"))
Description: Analyze Survey of Consumer Finances (SCF) public-use microdata. 
  Functions download prepared '.rds' files, construct replicate-weighted 
  multiply-imputed survey designs, compute descriptive statistics and model 
  estimates, and produce plots and tables. Methods build on design-based 
  inference for complex surveys and multiple imputation pooling. Key references 
  include: Rubin (1987) "Statistical Analysis with Missing Data" 
  <ISBN:9780470526798>; Barnard and Rubin (1999) "Small-sample degrees of 
  freedom with multiple imputation" <doi:10.1093/biomet/86.4.948>; Lumley 
  (2004) "Analysis of Complex Survey Samples" <doi:10.18637/jss.v009.i08>; 
  Lumley (2011) "Complex Surveys: A Guide to Analysis Using R" 
  <ISBN:9781118210932>; U.S. Federal Reserve (2023) "Survey of Consumer 
  Finances: Codebook" 
  <https://www.federalreserve.gov/econres/files/codebk2022.txt>.
